A||||20||william_thorniii||Passing a Fiero ??????||||2||
Z||000000||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||08:10 PM||||Friends,<P>What do you do when passing a Fiero?  <P>I am fortunate enough to live in an area of the country where Fiero's are abundant.  Every day, I see at least 3.  In fact there are 4 that I see on a regular basis in my neighborhood alone (There goes the neighborhood!).  My question is how do you react when you see another Fiero.  I usually give the standard (nifty fifties) thumbs up.  Usually the other drivers look at me like I have leprosy.  My fiancée also thinks I am an idiot for gesturing.  What do you guys think or do?<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||2
Z||000001||fiero56||03-10-2000||08:51 PM||||William, I don't do anything anymore. I used to give a thumbs-up or wave, but got so few returned gestures, gave up. Now I just stare at the Fiero as it goes by, owners notice and occasionally wave.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||03-10-2000||08:52 PM||||I stop driving, pull over and stroke it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||09:35 PM||||88formula,<P>Funny... but obviously you aren't a body man.  Remember one must NEVER under any circumstances touch a painted  and dry surface.  Sorry just a little flashback from my detailing days.  There was nothing worse than spending 8 hours buffing out tiny scratches and then seeing the owner (or dealer) walk up, see some lint on the car and proceed to rub it with their shirt sleeve.  It still makes me cry thinking about it.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000004||doughboySE||03-10-2000||09:36 PM||||88formula <BR>heheheheheheheh your hilarious <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">))))))))<BR>stroke yourself or the car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>HEY GUYS IN CANADA I WAVE AND THEY WAVE BACK<BR>just like the motor bike guys but see in canada we have to work harder to keep our babies looking good so we all appriciate the work each of us take on our cars||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||09:39 PM||||Way to go doughboy,<P>mmmmmmmm doughnuts!<P>Really though I guess I think there should be more comrodarie (spelling?) like with the old rods, customs and classics.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||03-10-2000||11:40 PM||||William, fiero owners out here like to stop and talk some have even flaged me down. If I can stop I will. Most are in nice shape so they understand what it takes to keep these little toys running and looking good. I try to give as much help and info as I can, but sometimes I do get some good info from them.<P>FIERO UNITY!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||stimpy||03-11-2000||12:01 AM||||In Oklahma Fieros are pretty darn rare (compared to California) and I usually get a wave or a look when I give them that distinctive Fiero honk.  The other weekend at the Sonic, I had some guy in an Accord wagon yellin to me through his window wanting to check it out. Turned out that he had an 86 GT too! But even seeing a sport ocupe in decent shape is a kind of an event in these parts. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||03-11-2000||12:29 AM||||Usually the drivers in beat up Fieros ignore me, but once in a blue moon I'll see a nice Fiero (usually when mine needs a bath). They'll usually wave at me and scope out my car while I'm checking out theirs.||||reg||1
Z||000009||wkayl||03-11-2000||12:29 AM||||Here in Colorado, I see 2 or 3 a day.  In my job I travel about 34,000 miles a year in the front range.  I have to watch the speedometer when I see one and am trying to catch up to it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||overlord||03-11-2000||07:56 AM||||up here in manitoba, canada<BR>fieros arent that abundant so when i see one and vice versa there is plenty of time to flip up the headlights for a quick flash.<P>so far in 2 years i have seen about 6 different fieros...so it is a real treat when i do see one.<P>now, where i live (very small town), people are always saying "there goes that fiero again" or when im crusing with my cousin "there goes that fiero and trans-am again."..what a pair...||||reg||1
Z||000011||RFMike||03-11-2000||08:53 AM||||I usually give the thumbs up, and get a response about half the time.  The other half of the time is discouraging, but I keep on giving the positive appraisal, even if the car needs work.<BR>If any of you guys are bikers and have toured anywhere in the midwest or west, you know that in the summer months, you get a thumbs up when you are out in the middle of nowhere from other touring motorcyclists.  Guys do it because they are sharing something most of the rest of the country doesn't have, and has no clue what they are missing. <BR>Sound familiar?||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-11-2000||09:08 AM||||William,<BR>        Here in East Texas I see only a few, maybe only once a month or so.... I just usually wave and about 75% of the time I get a response back.. You see here in Texas we are still friendly and wave back..lol  but serious.... I see only a hand full every 6 month's. I wish i saw more. OH I did see a nice red GT yesterday on HWY 155south, If it was anyone on the forum please respond so that we can get together and chat or something...              Steve||||reg||6
Z||000013||TheFiero64||03-12-2000||03:53 PM||||I usually give a thumbs up and wave. If going the other way I give a headlight wave. I don't get much response. Actually I've only got a response once and the guy stayed side by side with me for 10 miles waving back and forth. I don't see many fieros around but at least I see some.||||reg||9
Z||000014||Ferrari355||03-12-2000||04:15 PM||||i don't see many Fiero's in oklahoma either, and the ones i do see usually aren't in good shape. But there was a kid at my school who drove a red 87-88 Coupe or formula that was in excellent shape, it was very beautiful and that's one of the few great shape fiero's that i've seen in person. I usually don't say anything i just stare when one drives by b/c our fiero is crappy looking and so embarassing becasue it's a work car so we never take it anywhere far b/c of the Transmission but once we get that fixed we are going to paint it and replace the notchback, and then i'll make guesturs to them once we are in the Fiero.||||reg||4
Z||000015||Phil||03-12-2000||05:58 PM||||The only gestures drivers make to each other in New England usually are not of the friendly type.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Deer_Slayer||03-14-2000||11:33 AM||||In this area, I'll unually see a Fiero on every other drive.  Suprisingly, most of them have been 84 models in rough shape.  There are some others in decent shape though.  I've seen at least GT's around.  I don't wave or make gestures though.  Around here, they would try to sue or beat the crap out of you for that.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||ChadMan||03-14-2000||01:03 PM||||I usually give a friendly wave - or if there aren't other cars around, a quick honk and wave.  I get about 50% return waves and 50% slack-jawed stares.<P>I saw a couple of Miata guys pass one another and they both flipped their lights up and down.  Too bad we Fieroholics can't do that without stripping our headlight gears...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Racer 1||03-14-2000||03:27 PM||||I rarely ever get to drive along side another fiero down here in NM. But what really gets me angry is when I drive my GEO METRO to work I sometimes see this <B>HOT</B> chick in a red 86 coupe stock pass me on the same route. But when I drive my fiero I never see her driving here red coupe dangit. Most of the fiero owners around here dont take care of there fieros. ||||reg||8
Z||000019||william_thorniii||03-14-2000||05:51 PM||||Racer1,<P>That sounds a little like the famous Christie Brinkley scene from "National Lampoons' Vacation".  Too bad you don't have a Family Truckster, you could pick up all the chicks then!  LITERALLY!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000020||fieroshop||03-14-2000||06:04 PM||||Well I see at least two to three new Fieros a week and see at least 15 everyday.I guess it pays to own a Fiero Shop and work ( I mean play with them) on them everyday. What a rat race, I get to play everyday and you guys out there have to go to work. OH WELL!!! Can't have it all I guess.||||reg||12
